<hr>

<h2>PART 3 — Biomarker-Specific Sensor Strategy</h2>

<h3>A. LPS</h3>
<table>
<tr><td>1. Why tested</td><td>Gram-negative-specific marker; the <em>only</em> one of the three with a fully transferable published label-free SERS protocol (Wu, Zhao &amp; Zughaier 2021) &mdash; <span class="tag-done">[DONE, documented rationale]</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Current status</td><td><span class="tag-assume">NOT STARTED experimentally</span> &mdash; zero spectra exist for LPS anywhere in the reviewed documents</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Expected sensing mechanism</td><td><span class="tag-prop">[Proposed rationale, from literature]</span> Lipid A's six saturated fatty-acyl chains physisorb onto Ag; phosphate/carbohydrate groups give Raman contrast</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Direct SERS attempted?</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> Yes, first (bare Ag, "Sensor A" or current M0 substrate)</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Capture chemistry needed?</td><td><span class="tag-assume">Unknown, not yet needed by rationale</span> &mdash; LPS's own lipid tail is expected to adsorb without added chemistry</td></tr>
<tr><td>6. Proposed surface chemistry</td><td>None initially (bare Ag); if needed, no specific LPS capture chemistry has been proposed anywhere in the documents &mdash; <span class="tag-assume">open gap</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>7. Sample preparation</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[DONE as SOP]</span> 1&nbsp;mg/mL stock in pyrogen-free water, vortex 2&nbsp;min + sonicate 15&nbsp;min, serial dilution to 100/10/1/0.1&nbsp;&micro;g/mL</td></tr>
<tr><td>8. Deposition/loading</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> 2.0&nbsp;&micro;L/spot inside hydrophobic barrier rings, vacuum-desiccator or logged air-dry</td></tr>
<tr><td>9. Raman acquisition</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> 785&nbsp;nm, 400&ndash;1800&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1;, 30&nbsp;s integration (start), 3 accumulations, power level 10</td></tr>
<tr><td>10. Controls</td><td>Same-session blank (mandatory, first); water-only drop; R6G go/no-go gate; LPS on <em>unetched</em> bare Si (negative control &mdash; proves SERS, not ordinary Raman)</td></tr>
<tr><td>11. Replicates</td><td>9 spots at primary concentration, 5 at lower concentrations, 2nd substrate for reproducibility</td></tr>
<tr><td>12. Detection criteria</td><td>BOTH 989 and 1330&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1;, SNR&ge;3, &ge;3 pixels, &ge;5/9 spots, &plusmn;5&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1;</td></tr>
<tr><td>13. Optimization variables</td><td>Substrate architecture (bare M0 vs. Sensor A/B), integration time, concentration</td></tr>
<tr><td>14. Failure modes</td><td>HNO&#8323; over-strip damaging nanostructure (Sensor A); weak Ag retention after re-seeding (Sensor B); LPS itself simply not adsorbing</td></tr>
<tr><td>15. Go/no-go decision</td><td>R6G gate first (SNR&ge;10 at 1509&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1;); then LPS detection criteria above</td></tr>
<tr><td>16. If detection succeeds</td><td>Proceed to dilution series/LOD, apply optimized substrate to LTA/NAM, first real project milestone</td></tr>
<tr><td>17. If detection fails</td><td>Try Sensor B; if still negative, treat as informative (substrate-analyte mismatch even for the best-precedented target) and re-evaluate priorities with Prof. Ajay</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>B. NAM</h3>
<table>
<tr><td>1. Why tested</td><td>Universal peptidoglycan-derived marker, present in essentially all bacteria &mdash; the project's most scientifically novel target (no published NAM-SERS precedent exists anywhere)</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Current status</td><td><span class="tag-done">[DONE, negative]</span> Attempted twice (June/July batch, mean SNR 0.89; fresh 12&nbsp;Aug batch, no reproducible hit). Reference DFT+powder Raman work is mature and near-manuscript-ready.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Expected sensing mechanism</td><td><span class="tag-prop">[Proposed rationale]</span> Weak/no natural adsorption to bare Ag (no thiol/binding group); if a capture layer is added, boronic-acid&ndash;diol binding is the proposed mechanism, with acknowledged uncertainty since NAM's classic diol site is chemically blocked</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Direct SERS attempted?</td><td><span class="tag-done">[DONE]</span> Yes, twice, both null</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Capture chemistry needed?</td><td><span class="tag-assume">Likely, per root-cause analysis</span> &mdash; but not yet tested</td></tr>
<tr><td>6. Proposed surface chemistry</td><td>4-MPBA <span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED, not built]</span>; alternatives ranked but lower priority: hydrazide chemistry, cysteamine electrostatic, EDC/NHS covalent, MIP, biological recognition elements</td></tr>
<tr><td>7. Sample preparation</td><td><span class="tag-done">[DONE as SOP]</span> corrected MW 293.27&nbsp;g/mol; 1&nbsp;mg/mL = 3.41&nbsp;mM</td></tr>
<tr><td>8. Deposition/loading</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> 2&ndash;3&nbsp;&micro;L confined drop (coffee-ring fix already adopted)</td></tr>
<tr><td>9. Raman acquisition</td><td><span class="tag-done">[DONE, as-run]</span> 5&ndash;10&nbsp;s integration, power levels 5/10, 3 accumulations (12&nbsp;Aug batch); <span class="tag-prop">longer integration proposed given the superlinear SNR-vs-time finding</span></td></tr>
<tr><td>10. Controls</td><td>Same-session blank (missing for the 2-min substrate on 12&nbsp;Aug &mdash; a documented gap), R6G gate</td></tr>
<tr><td>11. Replicates</td><td>&ge;3 spots/condition (AgNO&#8323; series SOP)</td></tr>
<tr><td>12. Detection criteria</td><td>&ge;2 of 930/871&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1; primary bands, SNR&ge;3, &ge;2/3 spots, &plusmn;5&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1;</td></tr>
<tr><td>13. Optimization variables</td><td>AgNO&#8323; concentration (5/10/20/40/80&nbsp;mM), then NAM concentration (5&times;/10&times;), then capture chemistry</td></tr>
<tr><td>14. Failure modes</td><td>Structural (no binding site) &mdash; documented as the most probable single cause; droplet spreading; low effective near-surface concentration</td></tr>
<tr><td>15. Go/no-go decision</td><td>R6G gate per AgNO&#8323; group &rarr; NAM band count/reproducibility ranking &rarr; if still null after A&ndash;D groups, escalate to concentration series, then capture chemistry</td></tr>
<tr><td>16. If detection succeeds</td><td>Major project milestone &mdash; first-ever demonstrated NAM SERS detection; proceed to LOD/reproducibility</td></tr>
<tr><td>17. If detection fails (even after AgNO&#8323; + concentration series)</td><td>Documented as itself a clean, specific, publishable negative result supporting the capture-chemistry-necessity hypothesis; proceed to 4-MPBA</td></tr>
</table>

<h3>C. LTA</h3>
<table>
<tr><td>1. Why tested</td><td>Gram-positive-specific marker (thick peptidoglycan wall analog of LPS)</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Current status</td><td><span class="tag-done">[DONE, corrected null]</span> 14&nbsp;Aug apparent 1095&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1; signal reclassified NOT DETECTED (single-pixel artifact). Reference DFT fragment model exists but is statistically weak/unresolved (NaN branch).</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Expected sensing mechanism</td><td><span class="tag-prop">[Proposed rationale]</span> Lipid-tail physisorption (like LPS), plus a secondary electrostatic route via its anionic phosphodiester backbone</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Direct SERS attempted?</td><td><span class="tag-done">[DONE]</span> Yes, once, corrupted by a detector artifact &mdash; effectively an untested null, not yet a clean result</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Capture chemistry needed?</td><td><span class="tag-assume">Unknown</span> &mdash; bare-Ag has not yet had a clean test</td></tr>
<tr><td>6. Proposed surface chemistry</td><td>None initially; cysteamine SAM <span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED fallback only]</span> if bare-Ag clean repeat fails</td></tr>
<tr><td>7. Sample preparation</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> Fresh prep mandatory &mdash; aqueous LTA stable only 2 days at 4&deg;C; 14&nbsp;Aug stock age unconfirmed, may have contributed to the confusing result</td></tr>
<tr><td>8. Deposition/loading</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> Same barrier-ring/confined-drop approach as LPS/NAM</td></tr>
<tr><td>9. Raman acquisition</td><td><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED]</span> 30&nbsp;s integration (longer than the 14&nbsp;Aug run, per the superlinear SNR-time finding)</td></tr>
<tr><td>10. Controls</td><td>Same-session blank, R6G gate, <strong>mandatory despiking before any peak call</strong> (the corrective rule from the 14&nbsp;Aug finding)</td></tr>
<tr><td>11. Replicates</td><td>9 spots primary, 5 at lower concentration, 2nd substrate repeat</td></tr>
<tr><td>12. Detection criteria</td><td>BOTH a phosphate band (1080&ndash;1095 or 1225&ndash;1250) AND a lipid band (1450 or 1131), each SNR&ge;3, &ge;3 pixels, &ge;3/9 spots &mdash; a lone phosphate band is "possibly detected," never "detected" (because 1080&ndash;1095&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1; is not LTA-specific &mdash; also seen in nucleic acids and LPS)</td></tr>
<tr><td>13. Optimization variables</td><td>Integration time, concentration (500/100/10/1&nbsp;&micro;g/mL), later cysteamine functionalization</td></tr>
<tr><td>14. Failure modes</td><td>Solution degradation (2-day stability window), fixed-pattern detector artifacts (now guarded against), weak intrinsic adsorption</td></tr>
<tr><td>15. Go/no-go decision</td><td>R6G gate &rarr; despiked LTA detection criteria &rarr; if null, cysteamine arm</td></tr>
<tr><td>16. If detection succeeds</td><td>Second major milestone; proceed to LOD/reproducibility; resolve the NaN DFT-fitting branch to support interpretation</td></tr>
<tr><td>17. If detection fails (clean repeat)</td><td>Proceed to cysteamine-SAM electrostatic capture arm</td></tr>
</table>

<hr>

<h2>PART 4 — LPS First Prototype</h2>

<h3>Substrate architecture choice</h3>
<p><span class="tag-plan">[PLANNED, recommended in LPS_Substrate_Strategy, 16&nbsp;Aug]</span> The current one-step MACE process ("M0") couples silicon nanostructuring and silver growth into a single uncontrolled event &mdash; whatever Ag morphology forms, forms, with no independent control. The documents' own literature review found that both strongest published LPS-SERS benchmarks used substrates where Ag morphology is engineered <em>independently</em> of the underlying structure (evaporated silver nanorod arrays &mdash; not replicable here without e-beam evaporation). The proposed workaround, <strong>"Sensor A,"</strong> decouples the two steps using only chemistry already available: (1) a longer 10-minute one-step MACE etch to build deeper Si nanostructure, (2) an HNO&#8323; dip to strip the Ag deposited during that etch, (3) a short, dilute, independently-controlled AgNO&#8323;/HF re-deposition step (5&nbsp;mM AgNO&#8323; + 1&nbsp;mL HF/50&nbsp;mL, tested at 30/60/120&nbsp;s) to grow fresh Ag on the pre-existing nanostructure. This makes Ag density/morphology an independently tunable variable for the first time in this project.</p>
<p><strong>Why separate the two steps?</strong> <span class="tag-prop">[Proposed rationale from the documents]</span> Because the R6G data already shows the current coupled process gives strong but <em>erratic, non-monotonic</em> enhancement across etch times &mdash; evidence that the uncontrolled Ag morphology is the likely limiting factor for a weak, non-resonant analyte like LPS or NAM, even though it happens to work well enough for a strongly-adsorbing resonant dye like R6G.</p>

<h3>Complete fabrication workflow</h3>
<table>
<tr><th>Step</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Key variables</th><th>What to record</th><th>Acceptance criterion</th><th>Still to establish</th></tr>
<tr><td>1. Si preparation</td><td>Start from a known, consistent wafer piece</td><td>Wafer ID, piece size (~1&times;1&nbsp;cm)</td><td>Wafer ID, cut date</td><td><span class="tag-assume">Not established</span> &mdash; exact resistivity/doping/orientation of the Aug batch not re-confirmed in Aug documents</td><td>Wafer spec sheet cross-check</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Cleaning</td><td>Remove organic contamination</td><td>Acetone &rarr; IPA &rarr; DI, 5&nbsp;min sonication each</td><td>Sonication times</td><td>Visually clean, no residue</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Nanostructuring / MACE</td><td>Build Si nanostructure and (in the one-step case) deposit Ag simultaneously</td><td>AgNO&#8323; mass (0.170&nbsp;g/50&nbsp;mL <span class="tag-done">used</span>), HF volume (8.6&nbsp;mL <span class="tag-done">used</span>), etch time (2/5/10&nbsp;min tested; 10&nbsp;min proposed for Sensor&nbsp;A)</td><td>Bath composition, etch time, temperature</td><td>Visible dark/black surface</td><td><strong>HF stock concentration never confirmed</strong> &mdash; assumed 49% throughout, unverified</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Ag formation (Sensor A only: strip + re-deposit)</td><td>Decouple Ag morphology from Si structure</td><td>HNO&#8323; dip time (until visible Ag lift), re-deposition time (30/60/120&nbsp;s proposed), re-deposition bath (5&nbsp;mM AgNO&#8323;+1&nbsp;mL HF/50&nbsp;mL)</td><td>Visual color change at each step</td><td><span class="tag-prop">Proposed, not yet validated</span> &mdash; no acceptance criterion established beyond "visible darkening"</td><td>Whether HNO&#8323; over-strips the nanostructure is untested</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Washing</td><td>Remove residual reagents</td><td>&ge;30&nbsp;s running DI rinse</td><td>Rinse duration</td><td>No visible residue</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
<tr><td>6. Drying</td><td>Prepare for measurement without introducing artifacts</td><td>N&#8322; blow-dry (preferred) vs. air-dry</td><td>Method, time-to-measurement</td><td><span class="tag-assume">Not established</span> &mdash; no quantitative freshness window has been set</td><td>Storage/oxidation timeline for this specific substrate batch unmeasured</td></tr>
<tr><td>7. Blank characterization</td><td>Establish background before any analyte touches the substrate</td><td>Same settings as planned biomarker acquisition</td><td>Full spectrum, 3 spots</td><td>No spurious bands above noise</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
<tr><td>8. R6G validation</td><td>Confirm the substrate is SERS-active before consuming biomarker material</td><td>0.01&nbsp;mM R6G, 3 spots</td><td>SNR at 1509&nbsp;cm&#8315;&sup1;</td><td>SNR&ge;10 (go/no-go gate)</td><td>&mdash;</td></tr>
<tr><td>9. Biomarker measurement</td><td>The actual LPS detection attempt</td><td>Concentration series, spot count per Part 3.A</td><td>Full log per EXP-LPS naming convention</td><td>Per Part&nbsp;11 detection framework</td><td>Everything &mdash; this step has never been run</td></tr>
</table>
<div class="caution">No document establishes exact HNO&#8323; concentration/dilution for the Ag-strip step, or precise re-deposition bath temperature. Do not invent these numbers in the lab &mdash; confirm with Prof. Ajay or determine empirically with a small pilot before committing full biomarker material.</div>

